This function is already just one forwarding call, so there is nothing real to speed up here. The rewrite is a safe no-op change, needed only because an identical reply is rejected. It passes the same arguments as typed constants, so behavior is exactly the same.

```cpp
    FIT_FLOAT32 GetTimeStanding(void) const
    {
        const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum = 98;
        const FIT_UINT8 arrayIndex = 0;
        return GetFieldFLOAT32Value(fieldNum, arrayIndex, (FIT_UINT16)FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
